# Copy to .env and adjust. .env is git-ignored.

# --- limits (apply to both usecases) ---
SBX_MEMORY=4g
SBX_CPUS=2
# Wrapper fallback when unset here: 1024 (code), 2048 (pentest — nmap &
# parallel scanners fork many threads). A value set here always wins.
SBX_PIDS=1024

# --- extra CA certificates ---
# Colon-separated CA files (PEM/DER) trusted in the image builds and in the
# sandbox — e.g. the root of a TLS-inspecting middlebox. Same as --ca-cert.
#SBX_CA_CERTS=/path/to/root-ca.crt

# --- OCI runtime ---
# krun (default) runs sandbox AND proxy as microVMs via KVM: own kernel,
# own /tmp, own page tables. The boundary is the guest kernel against the
# VMM, a rootless host process without caps (inside the guest, --cap-drop
# and no-new-privileges do not apply). Requires `dnf install crun-krun` and
# an accessible /dev/kvm. runsc (gVisor) is the alternative user-space
# kernel. crun (plain container, host kernel) is supported but explicit
# only — the wrapper never falls back to it silently. The wrapper fails
# hard at startup if the chosen runtime (or /dev/kvm for krun) is missing.
# SBX_RUNTIME=krun

# --- external proxy (-p) ---
# Port harrbjorn's proxy is published on (127.0.0.1 only) as the external
# proxy's upstream. Burp: Settings > Network > Connections > Upstream proxy
# servers: destination host *, proxy 127.0.0.1:<this port>.
# SBX_UPSTREAM_PORT=3129

# --- terminal locale ---
# Locale the sandbox runs under (injected as LANG). It must be a locale the
# image generated: nb_NO.UTF-8 (default — Norwegian keyboard å/ø/æ in
# interactive mode) or en_US.UTF-8. To use another, generate it in the image
# first (code/Dockerfile locale-gen step). A value set here always wins.
# SBX_LOCALE=nb_NO.UTF-8

# --- model backend ---
# pi against an OpenAI-compatible endpoint (vLLM, llama.cpp, ...). Keep the
# real URL and key here in .env (git-ignored), never in the repo. A loopback
# URL (http://localhost:PORT) is rewritten to host.containers.internal and
# its port granted to the proxy as a trusted upstream; a remote URL opens
# its host — and, for a name on private addresses, those addresses on the
# model port only. vLLM: --api-key is the key, --served-model-name the
# model, and --enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser is needed for
# pi's tool calls.
# SBX_MODEL_BASE_URL=https://llm.example.net/v1
# SBX_MODEL=my-model
# SBX_MODEL_API_KEY=...
# Optional; pi assumes 128k/16k without them.
# SBX_MODEL_CONTEXT_WINDOW=131072
# SBX_MODEL_MAX_TOKENS=16384

# --- network egress ---
# Network access is a per-session choice on the command line (--net: hosts,
# @sets, host:PORT, @all for open egress); without it only the model
# endpoint is open. It cannot be widened here (SBX_OPEN_NETWORK is ignored).
